  "text": "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0$ and ${x}_{2,3}=1\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4x(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-x(1-3\\text{i})-x(1+3\\text{i})+(1+3\\text{i})(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-2x+10) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+40x & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+40x.$",
